  "summary": "The corner frequency: lower is darker for a low-pass; route an envelope here for plucks and sweeps.",
  "text": "filter1.cutoff (Cutoff) is a parameter of the filter (svf).\nThe corner frequency: lower is darker for a low-pass; route an envelope here for plucks and sweeps.\nIn Hz, from 20Hz to 20kHz, default 2kHz. Its knob is logarithmic: equal steps are equal ratios, so a turn near the bottom is as big a musical move as one near the top.\nWrite it as 800, 800Hz, 1.2kHz.\nIt mainly moves spectrum.centroid_hz: Average frequency of the sound's energy, weighted by magnitude (spectral centroid). Higher is brighter; a pure sine reads its own pitch.\nRoutes can modulate it (an LFO or envelope into this address), and host automation can drive it.",
